            "relation": "USES_PHYSICAL_SCHEME",
            "target_entity_instance": "power law damage function",
            "target_entity_type": "PhysicalScheme",
            "paragraph": "The effect of climate change on the efficiency of hydro- and thermo-electric power plants is represented in FRIDA, based on a literature estimate (Sect. 2.1.1). However, no suitable literature to represent the global effect of climate change on energy systems infrastructure was identified. This impact channel was therefore incorporated via an internally calibrated parameter (see Schoenberg et al., 2025a), with damages on energy infrastructure represented as a power law function of global temperature anomaly. This functional form was chosen based on its prevalence in IAM literature (F\u00fcssel, 2010; Nordhaus, 2014).",
            "ontology_conformed": true,
            "evidence_validated": true,
            "valid": true,
            "eval": true
        },
        {
            "source_entity_instance": "FRIDAv2.1",
            "source_entity_type": "Source",
            "relation": "USES_PHYSICAL_SCHEME",
            "target_entity_instance": "logistic function",
            "target_entity_type": "PhysicalScheme",
            "paragraph": "Similarly to how FRIDA calculates the increasing exposure of coastal assets, it also calculates the increasing exposure of the coastal population to SLR-driven storm surge damages using a logistic function (Ramme et al 2025).",
            "ontology_conformed": false,
            "evidence_validated": true,
            "valid": true,
            "eval": true
        },
        {
            "source_entity_instance": "FRIDAv2.1",
            "source_entity_type": "Source",
            "relation": "USES_PHYSICAL_SCHEME",
            "target_entity_instance": "linear function for evapotranspiration",
            "target_entity_type": "PhysicalScheme",
            "paragraph": "In FRIDA the impact of increasing surface temperatures on water lost to evapotranspiration during irrigation is represented on a per irrigated hectare per year basis. This is modelled using a calibrated, shallow linear function based on the GMST anomaly.",
            "ontology_conformed": false,
            "evidence_validated": true,
            "valid": true,
            "eval": true
        },
        {
            "source_entity_instance": "FRIDAv2.1",
            "source_entity_type": "Source",
            "relation": "INHERITED_FROM",
            "target_entity_instance": "FaIR",
            "target_entity_type": "Source",
            "paragraph": "Additionally, the deterministic climate response in FRIDAv2.1 could be developed to include a stochastic component, drawing on the representation used in the FaIR model (Smith et al., 2024), upon which the Climate module of FRIDA is substantially based (Wells et al., 2025).",
